  "summary": "Five candidate documents directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles (gradient boosted trees) to traffic forecasting. [V0231] (Gupta et al., 2023) evaluates on the AgriSat-4 dataset, reporting 0.85 accuracy. [V0230] (Fischer et al., 2022) applies the method to the Atlas-ICU dataset for road traffic flow prediction, achieving a test F1 of 0.78. [V0232] (Haddad et al., 2024) reports results on the LedgerGuard dataset with MAE=0.92. [V0229] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) uses the MetroFlow dataset and reports AUROC of 0.71. [V0136] (Duarte et al., 2020) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles but to electricity consumption prediction rather than traffic, making it the weakest match; it is included as the fifth candidate because no other document combines the required method with the traffic topic. Documents such as [V0225] and [V0226] address traffic forecasting but use decentralised training methods, not gradient boosted trees, and are therefore excluded. Documents that only mention boosted decision-tree ensembles for traffic in a prior-work context (e.g., [V0092], [V0010], [V0020], [V0022], [V0021]) are not direct applications and are excluded.",
